        "geoBonBiome": null,
        "geology": "The Salcher landslide is located in a geologically complex zone in the immediate transition area between the flysch zone, the Grestner cliff zone and the Northern Limestone Alps. The deeply weathered rocks of this area and their high proportion of clay and its weathering products are among the main reasons for the fact that this area has one of the highest susceptibility to landslides in Lower Austria and in Austria as a whole (see, among others, Gottschling 2006; Petschko et al. 2014).",
